# Which database JussiMiniPos opens, and how to reach it.
#
# Copy this file to "database.env" beside JussiMiniPos.exe (or into
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\JussiMiniPos) and edit it. The real file is gitignored,
# because it holds a password.
#
# Every setting here can also be given as an environment variable of the same
# name. The file wins where both are set: the file is what an administrator
# edits on purpose, so a stray variable in a shell cannot quietly point a till
# at the wrong database.
#
# Leave the whole file out and the application uses SQLite, which needs no
# configuration and no server.

# sqlite (default) or postgresql
JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_PROVIDER=sqlite


# ---------- SQLite ----------
# Where the database file lives. Defaults to
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\JussiMiniPos\jussiminipos.db
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_PATH=C:\ProgramData\JussiMiniPos\jussiminipos.db


# ---------- PostgreSQL ----------
# Used only when the provider above is postgresql.
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_HOST=localhost
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_PORT=5432
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_NAME=jussiminipos
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_USER=jussipos
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_PASSWORD=

# Or give the whole connection string yourself, which is what you want for
# anything the settings above cannot express — TLS, a connection pool size, a
# non-default schema. Set, it wins over every field above.
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DB_CONNECTION=Host=db.example.com;Port=5432;Database=jussiminipos;Username=jussipos;Password=secret;SSL Mode=Require


# ---------- Shared ----------
# Where product images and the Gemini API key are kept. Under SQLite this
# defaults to the folder holding the database file; under PostgreSQL there is
# no such file, so it defaults to %LOCALAPPDATA%\JussiMiniPos\postgresql.
#
# Those defaults are deliberately different folders. Images are files on disk
# that only the database knows the names of, and deleting rows sweeps away the
# pictures nothing points at any more — so two databases sharing one image
# folder means each one's sweep deletes the other's pictures. Only point both
# at the same place if that is genuinely what you want.
#JUSSIMINIPOS_DATA_DIR=C:\ProgramData\JussiMiniPos
